# STM32F411RE HAL LED Blink

This project demonstrates LED blinking on the STM32F411RE microcontroller using the STM32 HAL (Hardware Abstraction Layer) library.

## Overview

The program configures GPIO pin PA5 as an output and continuously toggles the onboard LED using the HAL GPIO functions. A delay is added between each toggle to create a visible blinking effect.

## Hardware

- STM32 Nucleo-F411RE
- STM32F411RE Microcontroller
- Onboard User LED (PA5)

## Software

- STM32CubeIDE
- STM32 HAL Library
- Embedded C

## GPIO Configuration

| Pin | Mode | Function |
|------|------|----------|
| PA5 | Output Push-Pull | User LED |

## Working Principle

1. Initialize the HAL Library.
2. Configure the system clock.
3. Initialize GPIOA pin PA5 as an output.
4. Toggle the LED using `HAL_GPIO_TogglePin()`.
5. Wait using `HAL_Delay()`.
6. Repeat indefinitely.

## Key HAL Functions Used

- HAL_Init()
- SystemClock_Config()
- MX_GPIO_Init()
- HAL_GPIO_TogglePin()
- HAL_Delay()

